.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/manuscript/output/
/manuscript/_quarto_output/
manuscript/bes.rds
manuscript/data/bes.rds
# Same file, after the restructuring into code/ -- contains the full
# extracted text of copyrighted papers, so it is never committed (see
# manuscript.qmd's own `data` chunk comment: hosted as a private GitHub
# Release asset instead, downloaded manually before rendering).
code/data/bes.rds

# Runtime caches from 01_run_metacheck.R and the reproducibility check
# scripts: speed up a local rerun but are not needed to render the
# manuscript itself, and can grow to tens of GB. Matched by **/ since
# metacheck.cache.dir is set to different roots by different scripts
# (code/data/, code/data/reproducibility_check/, ...), except the tiny
# fixture under vendor/metacheck/tests/testthat/, which is real test
# data bundled with the vendored package, not a download cache.
**/.metacheck_repo_cache/
**/.metacheck_repo_info_cache/
**/.metacheck_llm_cache/
**/.metacheck_zip_peek_cache/
!code/data/reproducibility_check/vendor/metacheck/tests/testthat/.metacheck_repo_cache/

# Per-batch checkpoint files from reproducibility_check/run_reproducibility_check.R:
# intermediate, regenerable via resume, not the final combined result.
/data/batches/

# Per-batch checkpoint files from 01_run_metacheck.R (and
# 02_run_open_practices_oddpub.R, sharing the same directory): only
# needed to resume an interrupted run; duplicate essentially 1:1 with
# the 3 final combined res_*_check.RData files once a run finishes, so
# committing both doubles LFS storage for files nothing downstream
# reads (the manuscript and comparison scripts only read the combined
# files, never these).
code/01_run_metacheck/batches/


/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
